sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch09-10> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Features such as seemingly continuous space and certain aspects of gravitation and quantum mechanics will emerge from many different underlying rules for the universe, whereas properties like the spectrum of particle masses, and perhaps the dimensionality of space, will be specific to particular rules.";
    dc:type "physical-hypothesis";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Space, gravity and quantum features are generic across many candidate rules";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 9, “Fundamental Physics”; section “Ultimate Models for the Universe” (from p. 465), p. 469. Scope: candidate fundamental rules for the universe"
}
